From 225f37dc20ed21c70ddac84154cfa07b35bc8f2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Leach <matthew.leach@collabora.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 11:17:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] [NOT-FOR-UPSTREAM] wireless: reg: don't load WW regdom from
 firmware

The regulatory.db file shipped in /lib/firmware contains an entry for
the WW regdom which prohibits passive scanning on 6GHz. This commit
skips any WW regdom queries to the regulatory.db file, falling back to
the patched static tables.

Signed-off-by: Matthew Leach <matthew.leach@collabora.com>
Signed-off-by: Henry Paradiz <henry.paradiz@gmail.com>
---
 net/wireless/reg.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/wireless/reg.c b/net/wireless/reg.c
index 0e13e4511ad1..fd26fab065b3 100644
--- a/net/wireless/reg.c
+++ b/net/wireless/reg.c
@@ -989,6 +989,10 @@ static int query_regdb(const char *alpha2)
 	if (IS_ERR(regdb))
 		return PTR_ERR(regdb);
 
+	/* Skip WW regdom in firmware file, falling back to the static table. */
+	if (alpha2_equal("00", alpha2))
+		return -ENODATA;
+
 	country = &hdr->country[0];
 	while (country->coll_ptr) {
 		if (alpha2_equal(alpha2, country->alpha2))
-- 
2.55.0

